# Trivy waivers for the frontend image scan (P17).
#
# GATE POLICY: the pipeline fails on CRITICAL + HIGH OS/library vulnerabilities
# (`trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --exit-code 1 --ignorefile .trivyignore`).
#
# PREFERRED FIX IS REMEDIATION, NOT WAIVER. The runtime image pins a clean, digest-pinned
# nginx base (`nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine`, alpine 3.23.x — see Dockerfile) that
# scans with ZERO CRITICAL/HIGH on its own, so this file holds NO active waivers. When
# that frozen base later accrues a finding, re-pin its digest (don't waive).
#
# Only add a waiver here when a CRITICAL/HIGH has NO fix available upstream AND is not
# reachable in our usage. Each entry MUST be documented: CVE id, why it's not
# exploitable for us, and a review/expiry date. Example (commented, not active):
#
#   # CVE-XXXX-YYYY  pkg foo  no upstream fix; <reason not exploitable>  review 2026-07-01
#   CVE-XXXX-YYYY
